ts / search bar** - Easier navigation helps users find products.\n\nI need to create hash codes using DJB2 algorithm:\n- Start with value 5381\n- Hash the What value and Why value together\n- Convert final unsigned hash to hexadecimal\n- Prefix with HDLmClass\n\nDJB2: hash = 5381; for each char c: hash = ((hash << 5) + hash) + c = hash * 33 + c. Then convert to unsigned 32-bit and hex.\n\nLet me define the improvements with What and Why fields:\n\n**Improvement 1:**\nWhat: \"Added a hero section with a clear value proposition headline, trust messaging since 1999, and a prominent Shop Best Sellers call-to-action button\"\nWhy: \"A strong hero section immediately communicates value and directs visitors toward purchasing, reducing bounce rates and increasing click-through to products\"\n\n**Improvement 2:**\nWhat: \"Added a trust badge bar highlighting Free Shipping, quantity discounts, rewards program, and 25 years of service\"\nWhy: \"Trust signals near the top of the page reduce purchase anxiety and give shoppers concrete reasons to buy from YogaDirect instead of competitors\"\n\n**Improvement 3:**\nWhat: \"Added percentage-off sale badges and star ratings to product cards\"\nWhy: \"Showing exact savings percentages and social proof via ratings makes deals feel more tangible and increases add-to-cart rates\"\n\n**Improvement 4:**\nWhat: \"Changed product call-to-action buttons from Select Options to stronger Add to Cart and Shop Now wording\"\nWhy: \"Action-oriented button copy reduces friction and ambiguity, motivating more users to begin the checkout process\"\n\n**Improvement 5:**\nWhat: \"Added an email newsletter signup section offering 10 percent off the first order\"\nWhy: \"An incentivized email capture grows the marketing list and converts first-time visitors into buyers through a discount offer\"\n\n**Improvement 6:**\nWhat: \"Added a customer testimonials section with quotes and star ratings\"\nWhy: \"Social proof from real customers builds credibility an