ss the original HTML directly, I'll need to reconstruct it from the text content, though the task requires preserving elements from the old HTML where possible.I've got the plain text from the fetch, so I'm working with just the extracted content about YogaDirect. I'll build out a basic HTML structure from this text, then layer in conversion-focused improvements like a compelling hero section with a clear value proposition and call-to-action button, marking all the enhanced elements with special hash classes to track what changed.\n\nI'm planning several key improvements: adding trust signals like free shipping banners and satisfaction guarantees, creating urgency with a limited-time promo bar, rewriting the featured products section with benefit-focused language, incorporating customer testimonials for social proof, adding a newsletter signup with a discount incentive, and computing DJB2 hashes for each modified element to generate the HDLmClass identifiers.I'm building the complete HTML page by merging the original content with the improvements, using hash classes to mark what's been changed, and outputting everything as a single-line JSON object.I'm preparing to output the final JSON response as a single line, making sure it's valid and matches the structure I've built.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm fetching the URL first, then I'll clean up the HTML and compute DJB2 hashes before returning the results as JSON.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The web_fetch gave me text instead of raw HTML, and the result type wasn't properly formatted—it came back as a JSON string. Since I can't access the original HTML directly, I'll need to reconstruct it from the text content, though the task requires preserving elements from the old HTML where possible.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I've got the plain text from the fetch, so I'm 