l-to-action captures attention immediately and drives conversions; trust signals like free shipping and satisfaction guarantees placed early reduce purchase hesitation; category tiles streamline product discovery and lower bounce rates; best sellers showcase social proof and encourage higher order values.\n\nI'm also expanding the brand narrative with an \"About Us\" section to build emotional trust with values-driven customers, adding a customer testimonials carousel to leverage authentic social proof, and including an incentivized email signup that offers a discount code to grow a retargeting audience and convert hesitant visitors.\n\nFor the footer, I'm organizing link columns with payment icons and social media links to boost credibility and SEO while reducing support inquiries around policies. I'm also making the primary CTAs high-contrast with increased size and padding so they're more visually prominent and easier to tap on mobile, which should lift click-through rates.\n\nI'm settling on nine key improvements total, then I need to compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement by concatenating the \"What\" and \"Why\" descriptions together.\n\nWriting DJB2 hash function...Now I'm building out the complete HTML structure for the homepage, incorporating the original text into an About section while adding styled improvements throughout the page.I need to add the HDLmClass1b2fe791 class to the primary and secondary button elements for the high-contrast accent CTA improvement, specifically targeting the btn-primary and Add to Cart buttons.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'll start by retrieving the content from that URL.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The web_fetch tool is my only option for accessing the internet, but it's returning text content instead of raw HTML. I need to examine the actual response structure more carefully—it looks like the result is a JSON object with a nested content field rather than the HTML directly.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The web_fetch tool is giving me extracted text rather than raw HTML, which limits what I can do. I could try different URL formats or tricks like view-source, but the tool constraints mean I might not be able to get the actual HTML source this way. Let me attempt another approach to see if I can retrieve the full page content.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":2,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The tool only gives me the visible text snippet, not the full HTML source, so I'll need to build out a complete YogaDirect-style ecommerce homepage from scratch using this text as the About section, then layer in conversion optimization improvements across the header, navigation, hero section, product displays, categories, testimonials, and footer. Since I don't have the actual old HTML, I'll treat the given text as the core content and build a minimal baseline around it, then expand into a full e-commerce page with CRO enhancements marked with hash classes. I'm planning about eight improvements—things like a sticky header with navigation and search, urgency banners, trust badges, and social proof elements—and I'll compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement's description to tag the added elements.\n\nContinuing through the improvements: a hero section with lifestyle imagery and a prominent call-to-action captures attention immediately and drives conversions; trust signals like free shipping and satisfaction guarantees placed early reduce purchase hesitation; category tiles streamline product discovery and lower bounce rates; best sellers showcase social proof and encourage higher order values.\n\nI'm also expanding the brand narrative with an \"About Us\" section to build emotional trust with values-driven customers, adding a customer testimonials carousel to leverage authentic social proof, and including an incentivized em