st badges highlighting their 1999 founding and free shipping, a featured products grid, the about section using their exact text, a newsletter signup, and footer with links and payment icons. Then I'll layer in conversion optimizations like a prominent \"Shop Best Sellers\" button in the hero, urgency messaging around free shipping thresholds, customer testimonials, an incentive-driven newsletter signup offering 10% off, and quick-action buttons on product cards to reduce friction.\n\nI'm also adding security badges near the footer, making contact information visible in the header, implementing low-stock indicators and countdown timers for urgency, improving mobile responsiveness with proper viewport meta tags, and strengthening the hero with a clear value proposition subheading. I'll mark each improvement with a class hash computed using DJB2 algorithm—concatenating the \"What\" and \"Why\" descriptions together, then hashing that combined string to create a unique identifier prefixed with \"HDLmClass\".\n\nWriting the HTML structure...","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":6,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I'm putting together the complete HTML structure with those classes integrated into the right places.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":7,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm catching a class name collision—I reused the same hash for both the trust badges and newsletter sections when they should map to different improvements. Let me trace back through the mapping to assign the correct class to the newsletter div. I'm seeing the hash mismatches now—I assigned 9b5a365b to the story-section when it should go to the newsletter div, and 589407c1 to the contact-bar when it should be on the story-section. I need to swap these mappings to align with the improvements list order. Now I'm mapping out the correct class assignments for each major section—the promo bar, hero content, trust badges, product grid, testimonial grid, ne