e an improved version that adds the viewport meta tag and other conversion-focused enhancements. I need to construct a baseline HTML document for the yogadirect.com homepage using the content I retrieved, then apply the single required improvement of adding the viewport meta tag. I'll build a complete but straightforward HTML structure with header, navigation, hero section, featured products area with the text I found, and footer, then add that viewport meta tag as the only modification.\n\nNow I'm computing the DJB2 hash of the concatenated What and Why text describing this improvement. The What explains that I added the viewport meta tag to the head section for responsive mobile display, and the Why details how the absence of this tag forces mobile browsers to render at desktop width, degrading UX and conversions, while adding the proper viewport configuration ensures correct scaling on mobile devices and improves SEO and conversion rates. I'll implement the DJB2 algorithm starting with the seed value 5381, process both strings together, convert the result to hexadecimal, and prefix it with HDLmClass.\n\nComputing the hash and generating the improvement record...I need to add a class attribute to the meta tag with the hash value prefixed by HDLmClass to mark it as changed, then construct the complete updated HTML document.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'll start by retrieving the content from that URL.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fetch is returning text content instead of raw HTML, so I need to examine the result structure more carefully to see if there's a way to get the actual HTML source or if the web_fetch tool is converting it by default.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I need to parse this result as JSON.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":2,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Web_fetch is t