ter\\\">\\n      <h3>Yoga Bolster</h3>\\n      <p>$34.99</p>\\n      <a href=\\\"/product/yoga-bolster\\\" class=\\\"cta-btn\\\">View Product</a>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"about\\\">\\n  <p>Thanks to our loyal customers, YogaDirect has become one of the largest suppliers of yoga mats and props in the country. We have been faithfully supplying the Yoga community since 1999 and are confident that we can help you grow your studio, event, or personal practice with everything you need and more. We manufacture and source our own goods which is how we can consistently offer high-quality yoga gear at amazing prices. When you shop at YogaDirect, feel proud in knowing that you are helping to grow not only your business or personal practice but the Yoga community as a whole. From our team of Yoga lovers to you, thank you.</p>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer>\\n  &copy; 1999-2024 YogaDirect. All rights reserved.\\n</footer>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Strengthened the hero headline and button copy to 'Shop Yoga Mats, Props & Gear' with a higher-contrast, larger call-to-action button.\",\"Why\":\"A clearer, benefit-focused headline paired with a larger, higher-contrast CTA button immediately communicates what visitors can buy and draws the eye to the next step, increasing click-through to product pages and boosting overall conversion rate.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass9bb9c1a\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'll start by retrieving the content from that URL.The web_fetch tool is giving me text-only content rather than raw HTML, but I need the actual HTML source. Since bash doesn't have internet access, I'm limited to the web tools, though they seem to convert everything to readable text. Let me check if the result object has a content_type or result_type field that might indicate HTML format, or if I can inspect the full response to see if raw HTML is available somewhere.I'm realizing I only have the extracted text content ra